// @expect-error 'id' is private to struct 'Key', so only code inside 'Key' can use it. Mark it 'public' to use it here.
// @expect-error A member is private to its type unless it is marked, so 'private' is never written. Remove it from 'id'.
// @expect-error build failed with 3 problems
// A member-visibility diagnostic names the owner by its real declaration keyword, so a
// struct's private member is reported as belonging to a struct, not to a class.
public struct Key {
    private int id;
}

main() -> int {
    Key key = {id: 1};
    print("{key.id}");
    return 0;
}
